From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] generate_initrd: release the DHCP leases before rebooting
 into the installed system

After a successful ISO install the launcher ran "shutdown -r now" and
the installer environment kept its DHCP leases. Its client identifier
(an RFC 4361 IAID+DUID) derives from the installer's machine-id, which
the installed system does not share. A DHCP server that binds a lease to
the client identifier - the VMware Workstation NAT DHCP server does -
then keeps the address of that MAC for the installer: it offers the
installed system the same address and NAKs its request until the
installer's lease runs out, so the installed system boots without IPv4
for up to the lease time and systemd-networkd-wait-online fails. Seen
with a 30-minute lease: the installer's lease ran its full term, and the
installed system got the address only after it had expired.

systemd-networkd sends a DHCPv4 RELEASE only when it stops a client
whose .network file enables SendRelease=, and Photon's default
99-dhcp-en.network sets SendRelease=no so that an installed system keeps
its address across a reboot. Neither the reboot nor stopping networkd
releases anything in the installer environment. Bringing the link down
does not either: the release is then sent on a link that is already
down.

After a successful install, and only then, the launcher now releases
every DHCPv4 lease networkd holds, one link at a time:

 - the leased links come from networkd's own link state, so several
   NICs, VLANs and a network configuration the installer applied are
   all covered;
 - each link gets a runtime .network file in /run that matches only that
   link, disables DHCP and enables SendRelease=; networkd reloads, stops
   the link's DHCP client and sends the RELEASE while the link is still
   up and still holds its address;
 - the release is confirmed from networkd's state (the link runs with
   that file and holds no lease any more) before the next link follows;
 - networkd and its sockets are stopped, which also releases any DHCPv6
   lease (SendRelease= is on by default for DHCPv6), and the system
   reboots.

Directory and files are created with umask 022, because networkd reads
them as its own user and the initrd's /etc/profile sets umask 027: with
that umask the files came out 0640 and networkd refused them ("Permission
denied"), so nothing was released.

Nothing reaches the installed system. The release is best effort: when
networkd is not running, a tool is missing, or a link does not confirm
in time, it does what it can, and the reboot happens in every case. A
failed install still drops to the debug shell with its leases intact.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 photon_installer/generate_initrd.py | 61 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 60 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/photon_installer/generate_initrd.py b/photon_installer/generate_initrd.py
index 53b1a54..71532b2 100644
--- a/photon_installer/generate_initrd.py
+++ b/photon_installer/generate_initrd.py
@@ -26,6 +26,62 @@ devtmpfs       /dev         devtmpfs mode=0755,nosuid 0   0
 """
 
 
+# Shell function for the launcher: releases every DHCPv4 lease networkd holds,
+# one link at a time, then stops networkd. Best effort: the caller reboots
+# whatever it returns.
+RELEASE_DHCP_LEASES = r"""
+release_dhcp_leases() {
+    local links=/run/systemd/netif/links
+    local prefix=/run/systemd/network/00-00-photon-installer-release
+    local state key value idx ifname dev file network lease tries
+    local -a leased=()
+
+    systemctl --quiet is-active systemd-networkd.service 2>/dev/null || return 0
+
+    for state in "$links"/*; do
+        [ -f "$state" ] || continue
+        lease=""
+        while IFS='=' read -r key value; do
+            [ "$key" = DHCP_LEASE ] && lease="$value"
+        done < "$state"
+        [ -n "$lease" ] && leased+=("${state##*/}")
+    done
+
+    for idx in "${leased[@]}"; do
+        ifname=""
+        for dev in /sys/class/net/*; do
+            [ "$(< "$dev/ifindex")" = "$idx" ] && ifname="${dev##*/}"
+        done 2>/dev/null
+        case "$ifname" in
+            "" | *[*?[]*) continue ;;
+        esac
+        file="$prefix-$ifname.network"
+        (umask 022 && mkdir -p "${file%/*}" && printf '[Match]\nName=%s\n\n[Network]\nDHCP=no\n\n[DHCPv4]\nSendRelease=yes\n\n[DHCPv6]\nSendRelease=yes\n' \
+            "$ifname" > "$file") || return 1
+        timeout 30 systemctl reload systemd-networkd.service || return 1
+
+        for (( tries = 0; tries < 100; tries++ )); do
+            network=""
+            lease=""
+            while IFS='=' read -r key value; do
+                case "$key" in
+                    NETWORK_FILE) network="$value" ;;
+                    DHCP_LEASE) lease="$value" ;;
+                esac
+            done 2>/dev/null < "$links/$idx"
+            [ "$network" = "$file" ] && [ -z "$lease" ] && break
+            sleep 0.1
+        done
+        if (( tries == 100 )); then
+            echo "DHCP: $ifname: lease not released in time" >&2
+        fi
+    done
+
+    timeout 30 systemctl stop systemd-networkd.service 'systemd-networkd*.socket'
+}
+"""
+
+
 class IsoInitrd:
     def __init__(self, **kwargs):
         known_kw = [
@@ -66,8 +122,11 @@ class IsoInitrd:
         script_content = f"""#!/bin/bash
             cd /installer
             ACTIVE_CONSOLE="$(< /sys/devices/virtual/tty/console/active)"
+            {RELEASE_DHCP_LEASES}
             install() {{
-            LANG=en_US.UTF-8 photon-installer -i iso -o {install_options_file} -e EULA.txt -t "{self.license_text}" -v {self.photon_release_version} && shutdown -r now
+            LANG=en_US.UTF-8 photon-installer -i iso -o {install_options_file} -e EULA.txt -t "{self.license_text}" -v {self.photon_release_version} || return
+            release_dhcp_leases || echo "DHCP: leases not released" >&2
+            shutdown -r now
             }}
             try_run_installer() {{
             if [ "$ACTIVE_CONSOLE" == "tty0" ]; then
